From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 16:25:42 -0400
Subject: D3D11: Release storage on zero-dimension base level transition

Back up existing mip levels to staging and release storage when base
level transitions to zero dimensions or mismatches storage, preventing
uninitialized GPU memory reads.

Test: angle_end2end_tests --gtest_filter="*BaseLevelChangeWithZero*:*BaseLevelZeroDimension*:*RedefineImageAfterZeroHeightBaseLevelTransition*"
Bug: b/561066220
Change-Id: I0722d601ecd564d44dd545796d8d775b38ee2bef
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8426123
Reviewed-by: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Ran Wang <wangra@google.com>
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
Adapted to the single gl::TexLevelMask releaseTexStorage() on M150: the
CubeFaceArray overload is not added and releaseTexStorageIfMismatched()
builds a plain TexLevelMask (all levels except `level`), which matches the
branch's prior per-type redefineImage() behaviour. releaseTexStorage()'s
loop keeps the branch's isImageComplete(index) guard. Because M150 ANGLE
still builds the D3D9 backend on Windows, TextureStorage9 gained the four
new pure-virtual TextureStorage getters (getLevelWidth/Height/Depth,
getFormat) mirroring the D3D11 implementations (depth is always 1 on D3D9).
angle_end2end_tests_expectations.txt kept as on the branch (test-only).

